   132	## A11.4 Dependency duty for registered decisions
   133	
   134	When a registered decision changes a parameter (an algorithm, a custody form, a channel, a horizon, a scope, a key),
   135	the owner sweeps the registered texts for sentences whose referent the change alters. Each one is recorded as
   136	amended, superseded, still fitting or open, before the decision's change is treated as complete. An owner decision
   137	that touches a registered parameter is checked against those texts before it is recorded.
   138	
   139	## A11.5 Results of the first sweep (2026-10-28)
   140	
   141	The sweep covered the original, Amendments 1–10, the freeze, the tracker and the author-rulings files
   142	(`docs/reviews/stale-dependencies/SWEEP-2026-10-28.md`). The owner checked each finding against its source. The
   143	review added item 3. The sweep did not read the rest of the frozen specification or the hybrid supplement
   144	(`SWEEP-2026-10-28.md:3-4`, `:20-21`). The Levadura panel read them. Its findings are §A11.3 rows 1, 2, 4–6, 8 and
   145	10–14, §A11.6 and §A11.7.
   146	
   147	**Scope from now on.** Every sweep under §A11.4 reads the frozen specification object in full (`spec.bin`: A9, A10,
   148	PROOF, V1-PROFILE, ENCODING-V1 and the hybrid supplement; `formal/freeze-v1/FREEZE-RECORD.md:16`), as well as the
   149	original, every amendment, the freeze record, the tracker and the author-rulings files.
   150	
   151	1. **H3 (`phase-0-prereg.md:232-248`): not amended.** H3 is a hypothesis with a stated falsifier. Its examples are
   152	   AWS-based, but they do not restrict it to AWS. It is measured over the whole deployed system, every provider
   153	   included. A measurement protocol is recorded before measurement. It covers retained resources (including the
   154	   compliance-locked trail bucket), defines the demonstration and idle periods, and reports the three numbers
   155	   separately. A slot-2 signer and an issuer poller that run through the operating window conflict with "idle
   156	   compute exactly $0". If that or another number fails, H3 is reported as falsified. The operating window is not
   157	   redefined as a demonstration to avoid this.
   158	2. **The slot-2 enforcement boundary: for the author's ruling.** A9.6 requires the final custody implementation to
   159	   be deadline-qualified (`phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:389-392`). The frozen record keeps "the selected,
   160	   deadline-qualified custody implementation" (`270ca49:docs/V1-PROFILE.md:1024-1025`). It describes it through
   161	   `prototype/policy-signer/` (:1033-1037), which met the deadline on 2026-10-14 (:1038-1040; §14.2 item 5,
   162	   :1429-1435). That qualification stands as historical evidence.
   163	
   164	   Production cannot run the prototype. Instrument code under `prototype/` stays instrument code, and service code
   165	   that ports it must earn its own evidence on its own bytes (`formal/freeze-v1/FREEZE-RECORD.md:62-64`). Nothing an
   166	   instrument produces discharges an obligation (A9:198-200). The E9 ruling R5b (`docs/reviews/e9-packet/AUTHOR-RULINGS.md:54`)
   167	   allows porting instrument code with evidence earned on the resulting bytes. It does not address A9.6's
   168	   deadline-qualified custody, so it does not settle this question. The registered texts do not say whether a
   169	   post-deadline port counts as "the selected, deadline-qualified custody implementation". Each reading keeps a
   170	   different registered text, so the author has to choose.
   171	
   172	   > **AUTHOR RULING: PENDING.**
